# Part III — Algorithms

| Algorithm | Description | Complexity / Status |
|---|---|---|
| **1 — Fidelity computation** | Computes \(d_{\mathcal{L}}\), \(\widetilde\phi_{ij}\), \(\phi_{ij}\), and the provenance state | \(O(\dim V_{ij})\) per pair; correct as a metric |
| **2 — Core extraction** | Computes \(\mathrm{Core}_\prec(k)\) by topological ordering | Linear in \(|V|+|E|\); conditional on fixed \(\prec\) and (OR-Xu) for identification with Xu’s core |
| **3 — Closure and injectivity check** | Verifies non-reconstructibility for \(A\subseteq Ess(G)\) | Conditional on (F1)–(F2′) and Lemma 2.4 |
| **4 — Confusable-block decomposition** | Uses **Allamigeon’s terminal-SCC algorithm**, not Tarjan/Kosaraju | \(O(\mathsf{size}(\mathcal{H})\,\alpha(n))\); computes terminal SCCs only |
| **5 — LWW join** | Key-wise max under the total order \(\preceq\) | \(O(|E|)\); correct under Lemma 5.3, without stamp uniqueness |
| **6 — GC safety check** | Verifies causal stability for \(OR\) tombstones and generation dominance for \(RW\) tombstones | Correct under Propositions 5.12–5.13 |

